WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.150
Kaze ni kami ga nabiku

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.150
My hair flows in the wind.

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:10.720
Kokoro ni hirogaru aozora no deai

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:10.720
An encounter in the blue skies of our hearts...

00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:15.980
Tooku hanaretetemo

00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:15.980
Though we are apart,

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:21.590
Kanjiru koto wa itsumo kimi dakara

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:21.590
I'm always thinking about you,

00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:26.930
Itsu no hi ka mune wo hatte

00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:26.930
so let's promise to meet again

00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:32.410
Au koto wo yakusoku shiyou

00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:32.410
one day, with our heads held high.

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:39.020
Zutto futari owari no nai

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:39.020
We'll be together, like a dream

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:45.410
Yume wo egaku you ni

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:45.410
with no end.

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:47.440
Kimi ni

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:47.440
I want

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:56.400
Kono omoi itsu no hi ka tsutaetai

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:56.400
to tell you this someday.

00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:07.370
Sabishisa wo shiawase ni kaeru tame

00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:07.370
I'm right here next to you

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:16.460
Soba ni iru yo kokoro wa

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:16.460
to turn your loneliness into joy.

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:24.830
Konna ni chikaku ni kanjiru

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:24.830
I can feel your heart so close to mine.

00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:36.080
Episode 23 - Showdown! The Two Helens

00:01:40.680 --> 00:01:46.170
The climax of <i>The Miracle Worker</i> sees deafblind Helen...

00:01:46.170 --> 00:01:49.280
realize that everything has a name.

00:01:50.660 --> 00:01:54.380
She lets the water trickle through her fingers and knows that its name is water.

00:01:55.440 --> 00:01:56.550
Water.

00:02:01.480 --> 00:02:02.800
Maya!

00:02:14.210 --> 00:02:20.210
Why does Helen only realize its name when she touches the water in the well?

00:02:21.420 --> 00:02:25.560
Why does she suddenly understand that it's called water?

00:02:29.540 --> 00:02:32.970
How do you learn your words, Helen?

00:02:42.390 --> 00:02:45.350
That's it! That moment there!

00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:49.620
The miracle occurs the moment Helen is taken aback by the water.

00:02:50.530 --> 00:02:53.470
I can do this. My Helen.

00:02:54.890 --> 00:02:58.020
Rain. Water.

00:02:59.370 --> 00:03:03.180
It's right there. It feels like it's on the tip of my tongue...

00:03:08.490 --> 00:03:10.480
Water... Water!

00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:17.610
Just then, the feeling of water rose up inside me, until it overflowed into words.

00:03:18.430 --> 00:03:24.270
That's it! The miracle needs a trigger to start it off.

00:03:25.900 --> 00:03:28.280
And then, the opening night finally came.

00:03:28.280 --> 00:03:32.220
The first girl to play the role of Helen is Ayumi Himekawa.

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:36.990
May I show you to your seat?

00:03:36.990 --> 00:03:39.750
Thank you, but I'm fine right here.

00:03:39.750 --> 00:03:42.930
I can see the show better from here.

00:03:42.930 --> 00:03:43.890
But...

00:03:44.770 --> 00:03:46.890
I'm going to stand right here.

00:04:08.340 --> 00:04:10.690
Please let go of her, Miss Sullivan.

00:04:10.690 --> 00:04:15.190
Let her do what she likes when she's eating.

00:04:15.190 --> 00:04:17.040
He's right, Miss Sullivan.

00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:19.760
Take pity on her and let her have her way here at least.

00:04:20.300 --> 00:04:21.880
Pity?

00:04:21.880 --> 00:04:26.970
Tell me, what good will pity do her when you've passed away?

00:04:26.970 --> 00:04:30.760
What you actually mean is that it's easier for you to spoil her...

00:04:30.760 --> 00:04:33.010
than to teach her anything useful!

00:04:33.410 --> 00:04:40.470
Unlike you, though, I can't simply sit back for six long years and not teach her anything!

00:04:40.470 --> 00:04:42.630
May I ask you all to please leave?

00:04:42.630 --> 00:04:43.720
Everyone!

00:04:43.720 --> 00:04:47.500
This child needs a firm hand!

00:04:47.500 --> 00:04:50.630
Please leave me alone with her.

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:04.010
Would you like some tea, little miss?

00:05:08.970 --> 00:05:11.050
I'm sorry.

00:05:11.050 --> 00:05:13.160
That taiyaki looks good.

00:05:11.050 --> 00:05:19.270
Translation Note: Taiyaki is a pastry in the shape of a fish, filled with sweet bean paste.

00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:16.250
May I?

00:05:17.860 --> 00:05:19.270
Why aren't you watching the show?

00:05:19.860 --> 00:05:21.690
Because I don't want to.

00:05:21.690 --> 00:05:26.130
I don't want to be influenced by Ayumi's acting - by her Helen.

00:05:27.170 --> 00:05:31.890
And yet, because of her being on stage, you can't leave the lobby.

00:05:34.450 --> 00:05:36.860
What is it about acting that captures your heart in such a way?

00:05:37.790 --> 00:05:42.450
Don't you ever think you would rather lead a more fulfilling life away from the acting world?

00:05:43.370 --> 00:05:48.430
I don't know. I don't know what makes me happy and what doesn't.

00:05:48.840 --> 00:05:56.660
All I know is that, when I'm acting, my chest swells, and I can feel my own courage.

00:05:56.660 --> 00:06:00.110
It makes me feel like I'm alive.

00:06:02.950 --> 00:06:04.180
I envy you.

00:06:04.180 --> 00:06:05.180
What?

00:06:05.680 --> 00:06:09.810
I used to eat these all the time when I was a kid. It takes me back.

00:06:09.810 --> 00:06:11.310
Thanks.

00:06:12.310 --> 00:06:16.850
Did he just say he envied me?

00:06:20.450 --> 00:06:23.840
The climax of the second act is coming up.

00:06:23.840 --> 00:06:28.010
Yes. This next scene is the crux of the play.

00:06:37.450 --> 00:06:40.270
You want to know what I'm doing, don't you?

00:06:41.640 --> 00:06:44.410
I'm eating with a fork.

00:06:48.350 --> 00:06:51.020
You are a very bad-mannered child!

00:06:51.020 --> 00:06:52.880
Your plate is over here!

00:07:07.340 --> 00:07:09.000
Your mother isn't here!

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:10.220
She isn't here!

00:07:12.270 --> 00:07:13.470
Helen, come here!

00:07:16.310 --> 00:07:18.020
This is your chair!

00:07:49.740 --> 00:07:50.810
Ayumi!

00:08:03.580 --> 00:08:07.020
Look at that. Your face is all dirty now!

00:08:19.840 --> 00:08:22.410
All this applause and it's only the second act!

00:08:22.410 --> 00:08:25.440
Yeah, we're doing well!

00:08:26.600 --> 00:08:30.380
Utako and Ayumi's mother-daughter combo will score us...

00:08:30.380 --> 00:08:32.270
the highest accolades at the Theater Festival!

00:08:32.270 --> 00:08:37.610
And that's when we'll steal <i>The Scarlet Angel</i> from under your nose, Chigusa Tsukikage!

00:08:40.550 --> 00:08:49.890
I want to teach you that everything in the world has a name!

00:08:49.890 --> 00:08:53.890
This is water! Water! This is water!

00:08:54.580 --> 00:08:57.850
W-A-T-E-R! Humans can crawl out of the darkness if they have the words...

00:08:57.850 --> 00:08:59.900
to express themselves!

00:08:59.900 --> 00:09:03.440
You don't have to suffer all alone in the dark!

00:09:04.790 --> 00:09:06.590
Helen!

00:09:15.060 --> 00:09:21.430
Water!

00:09:27.840 --> 00:09:30.470
That's right, Helen! Water!

00:09:30.470 --> 00:09:34.220
W-A-T-E-R.

00:09:34.220 --> 00:09:35.740
Water!

00:09:38.840 --> 00:09:42.470
That's it! That's it! This is water! You understand, don't you, Helen?

00:09:47.860 --> 00:09:48.980
What's wrong?

00:09:50.620 --> 00:09:52.350
Helen, you know me, don't you?

00:09:52.810 --> 00:09:54.600
You know her, don't you?

00:09:56.970 --> 00:09:58.320
Helen!

00:10:07.380 --> 00:10:13.230
T-E-A-C-H-E-R.

00:10:13.580 --> 00:10:15.200
I'm your teacher.

00:10:20.140 --> 00:10:22.630
That's right. I'm your teacher.

00:10:37.390 --> 00:10:39.680
You did a great job out there, Ayumi!

00:10:39.680 --> 00:10:42.440
Your Helen was sensational.

00:10:42.810 --> 00:10:46.430
One of the judges from the Theater Festival has spoken very highly of your performance as well.

00:10:46.960 --> 00:10:50.120
I'm sorry. I'm very tired today.

00:10:53.350 --> 00:10:55.620
I wonder what's wrong with her.

00:10:55.620 --> 00:10:58.010
I don't know. The show was such a success.

00:11:01.350 --> 00:11:07.850
I'm scared. Being judged next to Ayumi scares me.

00:11:16.880 --> 00:11:20.410
It's no good. I'm shaking.

00:11:20.410 --> 00:11:22.770
And the show's about to start.

00:11:23.300 --> 00:11:25.950
What am I going to do?

00:11:26.970 --> 00:11:29.590
Maya, hurry up and come with me.

00:11:31.200 --> 00:11:34.910
Miss Maya Kitajima

00:11:35.400 --> 00:11:36.870
Wow!

00:11:36.870 --> 00:11:37.980
Here.

00:11:41.040 --> 00:11:44.750
I will be watching your Helen. From Your Fan.

00:11:41.530 --> 00:11:44.780
He's here to see me. Mr. Purple Roses is here...

00:11:45.640 --> 00:11:49.760
somewhere in this auditorium!

00:11:50.380 --> 00:11:52.770
"I will be watching your Helen."

00:11:52.770 --> 00:11:56.090
My Helen!

00:11:58.360 --> 00:12:02.590
He's right: I have my own Helen.

00:12:02.590 --> 00:12:04.800
Only <i>I</i> can play this Helen.

00:12:06.100 --> 00:12:08.650
Thank you so much for coming, Miss Sullivan.

00:12:09.070 --> 00:12:10.630
Helen is over there.

00:12:13.470 --> 00:12:16.960
What's she doing? She's completely different from when we were rehearsing.

00:12:18.640 --> 00:12:21.520
That's Helen.

00:12:22.440 --> 00:12:24.470
Keep it together...

00:12:34.600 --> 00:12:37.720
Why? Why won't she move?

00:12:40.390 --> 00:12:41.800
Come on, move!

00:12:54.800 --> 00:12:57.280
Even though nothing's really happening in this scene, I feel all tense!

00:12:57.280 --> 00:12:59.340
Me too! I can't take my eyes off them.

00:12:59.340 --> 00:13:04.060
An actor who can provoke tension and relief will always grab the audience's attention.

00:13:07.250 --> 00:13:12.080
She doesn't know it yet, but she feels it instinctively.

00:13:13.000 --> 00:13:14.360
It's instinctual.

00:13:16.800 --> 00:13:21.260
This is a doll, Helen. D-O-L-L.

00:13:21.260 --> 00:13:22.310
A doll!

00:13:33.180 --> 00:13:35.620
Helen, you mustn't!

00:13:45.690 --> 00:13:49.730
What is she doing? She's supposed to hit me in this scene!

00:13:49.730 --> 00:13:53.580
Miss Utako is acting strangely, isn't she, Mr. Onodera?

00:13:53.580 --> 00:13:55.090
I wonder what's wrong...

00:13:56.620 --> 00:13:58.300
Helen!

00:13:58.770 --> 00:14:01.060
You have to learn your alphabet!

00:14:25.640 --> 00:14:29.340
How strange. You can see the darkness surrounding that girl.

00:14:29.340 --> 00:14:30.130
Come again?

00:14:30.670 --> 00:14:34.010
Even though the lights are on and the stage is fully illuminated,

00:14:34.010 --> 00:14:39.040
watching her movements, everything seems to be slowly absorbed by the darkness.

00:14:42.240 --> 00:14:44.530
This is a curious <i>Miracle Worker</i>.

00:14:44.530 --> 00:14:50.050
By merely changing the actress playing Helen, the whole play itself has changed.

00:14:50.050 --> 00:14:51.540
What the hell's going on?

00:14:51.540 --> 00:14:54.650
This girl's giving Utako Himekawa the runaround out there!

00:14:57.420 --> 00:15:02.510
Will you entrust the play to me, Mr. Onodera?

00:15:02.510 --> 00:15:03.680
What exactly do you mean by that?

00:15:03.680 --> 00:15:07.720
My regular Sullivan isn't sufficient to face up to this girl!

00:15:08.820 --> 00:15:11.930
I simply cannot act with her.

00:15:11.930 --> 00:15:14.720
What's supposed to be mere acting transforms into reality!

00:15:15.240 --> 00:15:18.430
Mr. Onodera, I am an actress too.

00:15:18.430 --> 00:15:22.020
For the success of this play. Please.

00:15:22.800 --> 00:15:24.220
Then, go.

00:15:24.220 --> 00:15:25.820
I'm counting on you.

00:15:26.350 --> 00:15:29.060
The stage is the realm of the actor.

00:15:30.850 --> 00:15:34.980
Yes, I'd like you to clear some room in tomorrow's culture column.

00:15:34.980 --> 00:15:37.460
Today's show is going to be headline news!

00:15:37.460 --> 00:15:39.330
What's that supposed to mean?

00:15:39.980 --> 00:15:43.580
What on earth is going on in there?

00:15:51.330 --> 00:15:55.760
D-O-L-L! Doll!

00:15:55.760 --> 00:15:56.940
This is a doll!

00:15:56.940 --> 00:15:59.430
What's going on?

00:15:59.430 --> 00:16:01.930
Miss Utako is totally different from when we were rehearsing.

00:16:02.320 --> 00:16:05.820
This is a C-U-P.

00:16:05.820 --> 00:16:08.740
A cup! This is a cup!

00:16:08.740 --> 00:16:11.850
What is she trying to do?

00:16:13.050 --> 00:16:15.980
Maya, you have your own Helen.

00:16:16.690 --> 00:16:19.870
That's right, I'm Helen.

00:16:19.870 --> 00:16:24.500
No matter what happens, no matter what anyone else does on this stage,

00:16:24.500 --> 00:16:26.070
I am Helen.

00:16:32.260 --> 00:16:34.840
This girl's stage presence is astonishing.

00:16:34.840 --> 00:16:37.520
She's responding to me with everything she has.

00:16:52.250 --> 00:16:55.210
Come with me!

00:16:55.210 --> 00:16:59.710
Their uncertainty at what the other might do next has created an unbelievable tension...

00:16:59.710 --> 00:17:03.270
that has enveloped the whole stage.

00:17:05.730 --> 00:17:08.530
Does this make you happy, Helen?

00:17:09.310 --> 00:17:13.530
All I want is to make you human!

00:17:15.210 --> 00:17:20.560
I just want you to sit on a chair and eat with a knife and a fork and a spoon!

00:17:21.810 --> 00:17:25.560
Helen! You're a human!

00:17:25.560 --> 00:17:28.360
You're a human being...

00:17:31.230 --> 00:17:34.890
I want to teach you that.

00:17:33.010 --> 00:17:34.890
She sounds so sad...

00:17:34.890 --> 00:17:40.340
This isn't acting. These words are coming out of Utako herself.

00:17:40.340 --> 00:17:42.000
That's how serious she is.

00:17:42.000 --> 00:17:42.750
What?

00:17:43.340 --> 00:17:46.630
The pretense has become reality.

00:17:47.310 --> 00:17:52.270
To go up against Maya's Helen, Utako has transformed into Annie Sullivan for real.

00:17:56.780 --> 00:17:59.950
W-A-T-E-R!

00:17:59.950 --> 00:18:02.390
Water! This is water!

00:18:02.390 --> 00:18:04.230
That's its name!

00:18:21.720 --> 00:18:23.290
What's going on?

00:18:23.290 --> 00:18:24.960
She's not moving.

00:18:25.510 --> 00:18:26.720
Maya...

00:18:55.600 --> 00:18:57.530
You understood, didn't you, Helen?!

00:18:57.530 --> 00:18:59.930
Yes, that's it! Water!

00:18:59.930 --> 00:19:02.300
This is called water!

00:19:04.960 --> 00:19:07.990
That's right. Mother - your mother.

00:19:07.990 --> 00:19:11.350
Father - your father. That's it!

00:19:12.920 --> 00:19:16.000
Helen, you really understand, don't you?

00:19:16.000 --> 00:19:18.390
Helen, Helen!

00:19:26.270 --> 00:19:30.300
Teacher. I'm your teacher.

00:19:35.700 --> 00:19:42.230
T-E-A-C-H-E-R.

00:20:20.450 --> 00:20:24.410
Miss Maya Kitajima

00:20:26.910 --> 00:20:28.830
Oh, thank you.

00:20:29.440 --> 00:20:30.670
Miss Utako!

00:20:30.670 --> 00:20:32.440
You did a fine job out there.

00:20:33.140 --> 00:20:36.190
What's wrong? Go and clean your face up.

00:20:36.190 --> 00:20:38.470
Yes. Please excuse me!

00:20:39.260 --> 00:20:41.190
We put on a good show today!

00:20:42.220 --> 00:20:44.910
I haven't felt such a sense of accomplishment in such a long time.

00:20:44.910 --> 00:20:48.460
Even though the play is over, my whole body is still radiating heat.

00:20:48.900 --> 00:20:51.760
In the beginning, I found acting with you very difficult,

00:20:51.760 --> 00:20:54.900
but there came a point where I was able to rise above acting...

00:20:54.900 --> 00:20:57.730
and I felt like I had really become Miss Sullivan.

00:20:58.040 --> 00:21:02.820
I really hated you, pitied you, wanted to save you, and thought:

00:21:02.820 --> 00:21:05.540
"I'm not going to lose to you!"

00:21:06.690 --> 00:21:09.770
I'm so glad I was given the chance to act alongside you.

00:21:09.770 --> 00:21:12.400
Let's keep it up, all the way to the final show, Helen!

00:21:12.400 --> 00:21:15.130
You got it, Miss Sullivan!

00:21:15.130 --> 00:21:17.440
I won't show you any mercy on the stage!

00:21:17.440 --> 00:21:18.470
Me neither!

00:21:20.180 --> 00:21:24.400
Were you watching, Mr. Purple Roses?

00:21:24.400 --> 00:21:30.320
I wouldn't have found my Helen if you hadn't given me that lift.

00:21:31.180 --> 00:21:35.550
Please keep watching me, Mr. Purple Roses.

00:21:39.120 --> 00:21:43.660
Acting News
This Season's Stage
Incandescent Thespians
What's Hot?! Fierce Contest in <i>The Miracle Worker</i>

00:21:39.590 --> 00:21:43.420
Maya and Ayumi have made it through the opening night of <i>The Miracle Worker</i> unscathed,

00:21:43.420 --> 00:21:49.750
but the fight between these two fated rivals has only just begun.

00:22:08.640 --> 00:22:15.370
From morning until night, from dusk till dawn,

00:22:08.640 --> 00:22:15.370
Asa kara yoru made yoru kara asa made

00:22:15.910 --> 00:22:23.310
you can feel the warmth of our love.

00:22:15.910 --> 00:22:23.310
Futari ai no ondo wo itsumo kanjiru desho

00:22:23.310 --> 00:22:30.000
All year round, every minute and every second,

00:22:23.310 --> 00:22:30.000
Shunkashuutou mo ippun ichibyou mo

00:22:30.830 --> 00:22:37.940
you can feel the warmth of our skin.

00:22:30.830 --> 00:22:37.940
Futari hada no ondo wo itsumo kanjiru desho

00:22:38.640 --> 00:22:46.190
This excitement is burning brightly like the sun,

00:22:38.640 --> 00:22:46.190
Kono dokidoki wa makka ni moeru taiyou

00:22:46.190 --> 00:22:51.480
Atsuku moete atsuku togashite

00:22:46.190 --> 00:22:51.480
let us burn brightly, let us burn until we're hot

00:22:51.480 --> 00:22:56.290
Koi wo shimashou!

00:22:51.480 --> 00:22:56.290
and make love!

00:22:56.600 --> 00:22:58.990
It's so Make it Make it Naked!

00:22:56.600 --> 00:22:58.990
It's so Make it Make it Naked!

00:22:58.990 --> 00:23:00.760
Make it Make it Naked!

00:22:58.990 --> 00:23:00.760
Make it Make it Naked!

00:23:00.760 --> 00:23:04.070
Sunao na mama dakiaou!

00:23:00.760 --> 00:23:04.070
Let's hold and be true to each other!

00:23:04.070 --> 00:23:10.570
Isso mekimeki nekki! mekimeki daisuki!

00:23:04.070 --> 00:23:10.570
And let's add more heat! I love the heat!

00:23:10.570 --> 00:23:13.960
Aishiae!

00:23:10.570 --> 00:23:13.960
Feel the love!

00:23:21.920 --> 00:23:29.030
Little one, I'm not the only one you've captivated with your acting!

00:23:29.550 --> 00:23:32.850
You and Ayumi have both been nominated for the Best Supporting Actress Award...

00:23:32.850 --> 00:23:34.340
at the Theater Festival.

00:23:34.340 --> 00:23:37.280
And you're the favorite to win the award.

00:23:37.980 --> 00:23:40.730
You'll experience lots of changes from here on out.

00:23:41.500 --> 00:23:43.380
You'll leave Ms. Tsukikage...

00:23:43.380 --> 00:23:46.660
and become a star for the Daito Theater,

00:23:46.660 --> 00:23:50.520
so that you can eventually spread your wings and become the Scarlet Angel!

00:23:46.750 --> 00:23:51.500
Episode 24 - Beautiful Maze
